.TH exmdb_local 4gx "" "Gromox" "Gromox admin reference"
.SH Name
exmdb_local \(em LDA hook that offers a exmdb_provider(4gx) client
with a C API
.SH Description
An LDA hook for delivery(8gx) which places mail into a store by
connecting to a exmdb_provider(4gx) service.
.SH Configuration directives
The usual config file location is /etc/gromox/exmdb_local.cfg.
.TP
\fBautoreply_silence_window\fP
-> See gromox.cfg(5) manpage instead!
.TP
\fBautoreply_subject_prefix\fP
-> See gromox.cfg(5) manpage instead!
.TP
\fBcache_scan_interval\fP
Interval in which to scan /var/lib/gromox/queue/cache.
.br
Default: 3min
.TP
\fBexmdb_connection_num\fP
Default: \fI5\fP
.TP
\fBlda_mrautoproc\fP
Perform meeting request autoprocessing after the rules of a delivered
message have run. Meeting requests are entered into the recipient's calendar
as tentative, room and equipment mailboxes accept or decline them according to
their booking settings, and responses and cancellations update the calendar
items. This needs lda_twostep_ruleproc. With lda_twostep_ruleproc=0, no
meeting autoprocessing takes place.
.br
Default: \fIyes\fP
.TP
\fBlda_relay_unknown_recipients\fP
-> See gromox.cfg(5) manpage instead!
.TP
\fBlda_twostep_ruleproc\fP
Selects the processor for server-side rules on delivered mail. With \fI1\fP,
the message is stored first and the rules run afterwards in
libgxs_ruleproc. With \fI0\fP, the older processor inside exmdb_provider(4gx)
runs the rules within the delivery transaction.
.RS
.PP
Compared to the old processor, the twostep processor also moves and copies
into other stores (if the mailbox owner has write access there) and logs
rule errors instead of failing the delivery. Its differences are:
.IP \(bu 4
After a move, the rules of the target folder are not evaluated.
.IP \(bu 4
SMS alert forwards (FWD_AS_SMS_ALERT) are sent as a short text mail to the
e-mail recipients of the rule. There is no SMS gateway, so recipients with a
mobile number get nothing and the rule reports a deferred error message.
.IP \(bu 4
Clients may briefly see a message in the Inbox before a rule moves or
deletes it.
.IP \(bu 4
Rules flagged ST_ONLY_WHEN_OOF are evaluated during Out of Office even
without ST_ENABLED, as MS-OXORULE v23.0 section 2.2.1.3.1.3 describes.
.IP \(bu 4
ST_ONLY_WHEN_OOF_EX, which Exchange 2007 sets on Out of Office rules, is
treated like ST_ONLY_WHEN_OOF.
.PP
The setting only affects mail delivered through this hook (LMTP/SMTP).
gromox\-import(8) \-D (without \-\-twostep) and messages saved into public
folders by clients always use the old processor.
.PP
Default: \fI1\fP
.RE
.TP
\fBresponse_audit_capacity\fP
Keep track of at most this many {From address, To address} pairs for bounce
reports in memory.
.br
Default: \fI1000\fP
.TP
\fBresponse_interval\fP
If a bounce report message for a delivery failure or operational failure is to
be generated, that return message will be suppressed if another report for the
given {From, To} address pair was produced within the given time period
previously.
.br
Default: \fI3min\fP
.TP
\fBretrying_times\fP
Default: \fI30\fP
.TP
\fBx500_org_name\fP
See gromox.cfg(5):x500_org_name.
.SH Notes
Out-of-office replies are only generated when one of the recipient's
addresses (primary or alias) appears in the To, Cc or Bcc line of the
message, cf. RFC 5230 section 4.5. Mail that reaches a mailbox only by way of
e.g. a distribution group thus produces no OOF reply.
.PP
Rule conditions on the message class of automatic replies
(IPM.Note.Rules.OofTemplate.Microsoft) only match replies that carry that
class, e.g. from Exchange in TNEF form. The Out of Office replies Gromox
sends arrive as IPM.Note.
.SH Files
.IP \(bu 4
\fIdata_file_path\fP/local_bounce/: response templates for when mail cannot be
delivered
.SH See also
\fBgromox\fP(7), \fBdelivery\fP(8gx), \fBexmdb_provider\fP(4gx)
